# Wave 5, brownfield. The canvas lines that make resize reachable.
#
# This is the whole reason the pillar exists. Everything resize needs has been
# in the tree since wave 3 and none of it runs, because canvas.tsx never asks
# whether the pointer is on a handle. routePress has had a `resize` branch and
# an `onHandle` field since wave 4; the canvas has never set the field, so the
# branch is dead and so is everything behind it.

file: "packages/editor/src/canvas/canvas.tsx"
doc: "The single SVG scene; a thin adapter feeding pointer and wheel events to the gesture layer."

constants: [
  { name: "Canvas"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Additions to the existing component. The SVG structure, the layers, the\n"
      "ResizeObserver, fit-on-load, the wheel handler and the error banner are\n"
      "unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "PRESS. Before routePress, ask handleAtPoint for the handle under the\n"
      "pointer, passing the current selection and a radius of `8 / zoom`, and\n"
      "hand the result to routePress as `onHandle`. This one line is what has\n"
      "been missing.\n"
      "\n"
      "That radius is 8 SCREEN pixels expressed in diagram units, which is\n"
      "what handleAtPoint takes. It is deliberately generous: overlay_layer\n"
      "draws each handle as a square of side `8 / zoom`, so the drawn square\n"
      "reaches 4 screen pixels from its centre and the grab radius reaches 8.\n"
      "The grabbable area is twice the drawn one in every direction, at every\n"
      "zoom, because a handle that needs pixel-exact aim reads as broken.\n"
      "\n"
      "PENDING. The gesture union gains a `resize` arm holding a\n"
      "ResizeSession. The session's ref is the single selected element and\n"
      "its origin is the diagram-space press point.\n"
      "\n"
      "MOVE. The resize arm feeds resizeUpdate into the same `preview`\n"
      "signal the move arm uses; OverlayLayer already draws it.\n"
      "event.shiftKey is read on each move, not captured at press -- the user\n"
      "presses Shift partway through a drag, which is when it is useful.\n"
      "\n"
      "UP. resizeCommit's edit goes through state.applyStyleEdit, like\n"
      "moveCommit's. A press that never crossed exceedsThreshold commits\n"
      "nothing.\n"
      "\n"
      "CURSOR. cursorFor takes a fourth argument, `handle`, and the canvas has\n"
      "never passed it, so hovering a handle shows the move cursor and every\n"
      "directional cursor in that function is unreachable. Track the handle\n"
      "under the pointer in a signal, updated on hover in onPointerMove\n"
      "alongside setHover, and pass it. During an active resize the signal\n"
      "holds the session's handle instead, so the cursor does not flicker back\n"
      "when the pointer outruns the handle it is dragging.\n"
      "\n"
      "moveUpdate and moveCommit lose their `zoom` argument; the two call\n"
      "sites drop it and keep passing the diagram-space point they already\n"
      "pass. Nothing else about the move path changes."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<CanvasProps>" } }
    uses: [
      "routePress", "exceedsThreshold", "panUpdate", "moveUpdate", "moveCommit",
      "marqueeUpdate", "marqueeCommit", "resizeUpdate", "resizeCommit",
      "applyWheel", "handleKeyDown", "DiagramLayer", "GhostLayer",
      "OverlayLayer", "hitTestPoint", "handleAtPoint", "screenToDiagram",
      "fitBoundsToRect", "cursorFor"
    ]
  }
]
